WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.240
A lift.

2
00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:05.630
The sign by the door says maximum
six hundred and forty kilograms.

3
00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.330
Eight people step in.

4
00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.050
Each one wears a label: eighty kilograms,

5
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.200
to the nearest ten kilograms.

6
00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:14.940
Eight times eighty is
six hundred and forty.

7
00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.620
Exactly the limit.

8
00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:18.350
So are they safe?

9
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.790
Or could this lift be overloaded?

10
00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:25.280
In this mission, you'll round to decimal
places and to significant figures.

11
00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:29.210
You'll estimate a calculation
by rounding every number first.

12
00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.980
And you'll find the bounds
of a rounded measurement:

13
00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:34.690
the lowest and highest values it could be.

14
00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:38.190
Your mission: decide whether
the lift could be overloaded.
